* soft-start-loop-gain -- klt sim circuit body template, DC hand-over deck (issue #451).
*
* tb_ss_handover.spice.in's circuit as a plain operating-point job: the deck is
* `op`-only (a `foreach` over V(SSR) with `alter Vssr dc` and an `op` each), so
* it has no `tian` analogue and is NOT approximated by one. Instead each ramp
* state is a row of the request's `corners.params` axis (`vssr`, zipped with the
* supply `vsup`), `analysis.kind` is `op`, and the HOV fields are `expr`
* measurements. Same circuit, same loop break (Vinj a DC short), same 36 ohm
* resistive load as the margin deck's `ramp` phase.

.include "dut.spice"

Vin VIN 0 DC {vsup}
Ven EN 0 DC {vsup}
Vref VREF 0 DC 1.2
.param vsup=3.3
.param vssr=0

Xdut VIN VOUT EN 0 AINJ BINJ VREF SSRPIN ldo_core
Vinj AINJ BINJ DC 0 AC 0

Vssr SSRPIN 0 DC {vssr}

Rload VOUT NLD 36.0
Vlmeas NLD 0 DC 0
Resr VOUT NESR 0.001
Cout NESR 0 1e-6

.model dclamp d(is=1e-14 cjo=0 tt=0 n=1 rs=0)
Dclamp 0 VOUT dclamp
